how_to_run:
1) Copy .env.example to .env and set DOCUMENTDB_URI to your cluster's SRV/TLS connection string. Optionally change CONSENT_RETENTION_DAYS.
2) Install dependencies: pip install -r requirements.txt
3) Seed sample data and ensure indexes: python scripts/seed.py
   This will upsert 3 sample customers into the database sample_customer_360_11.consents and create the TTL index.
4) Start the app for manual testing: uvicorn app.main:app --reload (note: see open_issues about Motor/PyMongo compatibility if startup fails; adjust pinned packages as needed)
5) API endpoints:
   - POST /consents/record  {customerId, channels, actor?, reason?}
   - POST /consents/withdraw {customerId, channels? (omit to withdraw all), actor?, reason?}
   - GET  /consents/{customerId}
6) Cleanup: remove documents via your Mongo client or the Azure Portal if desired.
